{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And against all the gods of Egypt.</b> Like 'I have made you Elohim to Pharaoh'; 'where the Elohim went.' The meaning of <b>against all the gods of Egypt</b> is the patrons of Egypt." "<b>I will execute judgments.</b> Torments, like 'and they executed judgments in Joash.' A house in which there was a firstborn — the firstborn is struck; if there is no firstborn, the eldest of the house is struck. And one should not explain 'Elohim' in the sense of idolatry, since it is not fitting to speak of torments regarding something that has no living spirit. Here Rashi commented: of molten metal, it melted and dissolved — like 'and the sun was hot and it melted.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:11.768910587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}